A||N||3||Monkeyman||Is there a longer heater control cable?||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-20-2001||11:49 AM||||The stock heater control cable is barely long enough for my new center console.  Is there another one (either aftermarket or from another vehicle) that is longer (by at least 3-4" to be safe) that will work?  I don't want to have to modify anything under the dash, if possible.  If nothing else will work, is there any place to find a slider control only?  No switches/knobs, just the slider.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroBUZZ||10-20-2001||02:33 PM||||MM:   I'd try a full size GM or even a GM Van or truck which may have a longer cable.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-20-2001||02:49 PM||||Thanx.  Can I assume that they all attach the same at both ends?||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-20-2001||08:00 PM||||Heater "cable" is pretty much the same for all cars that use it. IE hard plastic jacket and solid wire rod... There's some variation in mounting but many can be used to replace the one you have. <P>You should be able to find a suitable one in many differant cars.<P>Take the stock one and make sure whatever one you use allows some adjustment on one and and that the range of movement is the same or fairly close.<P>Make sure the one you find doesn't need to be twisted for the anchors to line up. More than a couple degrees twisting will make it bind or break the anchors.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
